"一个主张成立必须具备的几个条件，缺一个都不行。把证据按要件一一对上，叫“组证据链”。":"The several conditions a claim must meet; miss one and it fails. Matching evidence to each element one by one is called \"building the chain of evidence.\"",
"一个理性的人在同样情况下应有的小心程度。明知有风险、有能力处理却放着不管，通常就是违反了注意义务。":"The care a reasonable person would exercise in the same situation. Knowing of a risk and being able to handle it, yet leaving it alone, is usually a breach of the duty of care.",
"一些国家和企业在月面作业时划出的“请别靠太近”的范围。它是协调手段还是排他领地，各方看法不同，目前没有统一规则。":"A \"please keep your distance\" zone marked out by States and companies working on the Moon. Whether it is a coordination device or exclusive territory, views differ, and there is no uniform rule at present.",
"不可抗力":"Force majeure",
"不能预见、不能避免、不能克服的意外。在很多合同里可以免责，但在《责任公约》的绝对责任下，它不是免责理由。":"An event that can be neither foreseen, avoided nor overcome. It excuses performance under many contracts, but under the Liability Convention's absolute liability it is no excuse.",
"专门管“太空东西把人砸了怎么赔”的条约。它把损害分成两种：砸在地面上的，和在太空里撞上的，规则不一样。":"The treaty that governs \"compensation when things from space hit people.\" It divides damage into two kinds: hitting the ground, and colliding in space; the rules differ.",
"举证责任":"Burden of proof",
"今天的决定会影响还没出生的人。2024 年联合国大会通过了《子孙后代问题宣言》，要求各国在决策时考虑他们的利益。":"Today's decisions affect people not yet born. In 2024 the UN General Assembly adopted the Declaration on Future Generations, requiring States to consider their interests when deciding.",
"以前的裁决。仲裁庭不受先例严格约束，但会认真参考；律师常引用先例来说服仲裁庭。":"Past awards. A tribunal is not strictly bound by precedent but consults it seriously; counsel often cites precedent to persuade the tribunal.",
"仲裁一裁终局，不能上诉。不服只能走几条很窄的程序通道：请求解释、更正笔误、补充漏裁，或者以程序问题申请撤销。":"Arbitration is final at one hearing; there is no appeal. Discontent has only a few narrow procedural routes: interpretation, correction of clerical errors, an additional award on omissions, or setting aside on procedural grounds.",
"仲裁与诉讼的通行规则":"The common rules of arbitration and litigation",
"仲裁庭亲自到现场去看。仲裁员可以提问、可以测量，但只能就本案争议点调查。":"The tribunal goes to look at the site itself. Arbitrators may ask questions and take measurements, but may investigate only the points in dispute.",
"仲裁庭判了当事人没有提交给它的事项。比如双方只请仲裁庭判赔偿，仲裁庭却顺手宣布了某块地归谁。超出的部分可以被撤销。":"The tribunal decided a matter the parties did not submit to it. For example, the parties asked only for compensation, and the tribunal also declared who owns a piece of ground. The excess may be set aside.",
"仲裁或司法机构就一个法律问题给出的权威看法。它不是判谁输谁赢，而是说清楚规则是什么。":"An authoritative view on a legal question from an arbitral or judicial body. It does not decide who wins; it states clearly what the rule is.",
"任何国家都不能把月球、小行星或太空的某一块宣布为自己的领土，不管是插旗、占领还是别的办法。":"No State may declare the Moon, an asteroid, or any part of space to be its territory, whether by planting a flag, occupation, or any other means.",
"你的活动妨碍了别人的正常活动。在频率领域，指信号互相打架；在太空活动里，指物理上的妨碍。发现可能造成有害干扰，应先协商。":"Your activity interferes with someone else's normal activity. In frequency terms, signals clashing; in space activity, physical interference. Where harmful interference is possible, consult first.",
"做事时要照顾到别人在同一地方的正当活动，不能只顾自己。比如在月球上作业，扬起的尘土不能毁了邻居的仪器。":"In acting, have regard for others' legitimate activity in the same place; do not think only of yourself. Working on the Moon, the dust you raise must not ruin your neighbour's instruments.",
"先申报先协调":"First to file, first to coordinate",
"减少新增太空垃圾的做法：任务结束后把卫星推离拥挤轨道、排空剩余燃料防止爆炸等。联合国外空委 2007 年出过一份指南。":"Practices that reduce new space junk: at mission's end, push satellites out of crowded orbits, empty residual fuel to prevent explosions, and so on. COPUOS issued guidelines in 2007.",
"卫星用的轨道位置和频率由国际电联统一协调：先提交资料的先排队，但要在期限内真正投入使用，否则要退回。":"Orbital slots and frequencies used by satellites are coordinated by the ITU: whoever files first queues first, but must actually put them to use within the time limit, or give them back.",
"双方自己谈妥，不再让仲裁庭判。好处是快、稳；代价是仲裁庭不会就法律问题表态，也就不会留下可供后人参考的说法。":"The two sides agree among themselves and stop asking the tribunal to decide. The upside is speed and safety; the cost is that the tribunal takes no position on the law, so no statement is left for those who come after.",
"发射或促成发射的国家，以及提供发射场地或设施的国家。一个物体可能有好几个发射国，它们一起负责。":"The State that launches or procures the launch, and the State from whose territory or facility the launch is made. One object may have several launching States, and they answer together.",
"只能以程序问题为由，比如仲裁庭没有管辖权、一方没机会陈述、仲裁庭判了双方没请求判的事（超裁）。觉得判得不对，不是撤销理由。":"Only procedural grounds count: the tribunal lacked jurisdiction, a party had no chance to be heard, or the tribunal decided what the parties did not ask it to (excess of jurisdiction). Thinking the award is wrong is not a ground for setting aside.",
"只要损害发生了，就要赔，不问你有没有错。《责任公约》第二条规定：太空物体砸到地面或飞行中的飞机，发射国承担绝对责任。":"Where damage occurs, compensation follows, fault or no fault. Article II of the Liability Convention: where a space object hits the ground or an aircraft in flight, the launching State is absolutely liable.",
