"在绝对责任下，发射国几乎没有退路。唯一的例外是：损害完全或部分是受害方自己“重大过失”或故意造成的。天气、太阳风暴都不在例外之列。":"Under absolute liability the launching State has almost no way out. The only exception: the damage resulted wholly or partly from the victim's own \"gross negligence\" or intent. Weather and solar storms are not exceptions.",
"外空条约":"Outer Space Treaty",
"如果一国认为自己的活动可能对别国造成有害干扰，应当先和对方商量；反过来，担心受影响的国家也可以要求协商。":"Where a State believes its activity may cause harmful interference to another, it should consult the other side first; conversely, a State worried about being affected may request consultation.",
"常见的仲裁程序":"The usual arbitral procedure",
"常设仲裁法院《外空活动争端仲裁任择规则》第36条":"PCA Optional Rules for Arbitration of Disputes relating to Outer Space Activities, Article 36",
"律师的基本功：指出“那个先例和本案情况不同，所以不该照搬”。比如前案是地面损害，本案是在轨碰撞，规则本来就不一样。":"A lawyer's basic move: pointing out that \"the precedent differs from this case, so it should not be copied across.\" The earlier case was surface damage, this one an in-orbit collision; the rules were never the same.",
"把某个太空物体登记在本国名册上的国家。它对这个物体保有管辖权和控制权，哪怕物体已经报废。":"The State that has registered a space object on its own registry. It keeps jurisdiction and control over that object, even once the object is dead.",
"损害确实是这件事造成的。要把“发生了什么”和“谁造成的”连起来，中间不能断。":"The damage really was caused by this event. You must connect \"what happened\" to \"who caused it,\" without a break in between.",
"探索和利用太空要为所有国家谋福利，不论经济和科技发展水平如何。这是《外空条约》第一条开篇就写的话。":"The exploration and use of space shall be for the benefit of all countries, whatever their economic or scientific development. These are the opening words of Article I of the Outer Space Treaty.",
"撤销裁决":"Setting aside the award",
"文化遗址":"Cultural heritage sites",
"早期登月着陆器、脚印这类有历史意义的地点。目前国际上没有专门的保护条约，但已有不少国家主张保护。":"Places of historic significance such as early lunar landers and footprints. There is no dedicated protective treaty yet, though a good many States have argued for protection.",
"普通法与仲裁实践":"Common law and arbitral practice",
"月球、小行星上的水冰、金属等。一些国家立法允许企业开采并拥有采出来的资源；也有国家认为这需要国际规则。开采和“占领天体”是不是一回事，至今有争议。":"Water ice, metals and the like on the Moon and asteroids. Some States have legislated to let companies extract and own what they extract; others think international rules are needed. Whether extraction and \"occupying a celestial body\" are the same thing remains disputed.",
"有害干扰":"Harmful interference",
"有错才赔。太空里两个物体相撞，受害方要证明对方“有过错”，才能拿到赔偿。":"Compensation only on fault. Where two objects collide in space, the victim must show the other side was \"at fault\" to recover.",
