"2009 年 11 月":"November 2009",
"2009 年 2 月 10 日，美国铱星 33 号与俄罗斯已退役的宇宙-2251 号在西伯利亚上空约 790 公里处相撞，这是第一次两颗完整卫星意外相撞，产生了上千块可追踪碎片。事后没有任何一方依《责任公约》索赔，一个重要原因是：在轨损害要证明“过错”，而当时并没有公认的避碰规则。2007 年联合国认可了《空间碎片减缓准则》，2019 年外空委又通过了《外空活动长期可持续性准则》，都不具强制力。据 SpaceX 公开的报告，2024 年 12 月到 2025 年 5 月的半年里，星链卫星做了约 14 万次避碰机动。<br><b>游戏里改动的地方：</b>国家、公司、“十七次预警”和“轨道数据过期”都是虚构的。":"On 10 February 2009, the American Iridium 33 and the retired Russian Kosmos-2251 collided about 790 km above Siberia, the first accidental collision of two intact satellites, producing over a thousand trackable fragments. No side claimed afterwards under the Liability Convention, and one important reason was this: in-orbit damage requires proof of \"fault,\" and at the time there was no generally accepted collision-avoidance rule. In 2007 the UN endorsed the Space Debris Mitigation Guidelines, and in 2019 COPUOS adopted the Guidelines for the Long-term Sustainability of Outer Space Activities; neither is mandatory. According to SpaceX's public reports, from December 2024 to May 2025 Starlink satellites performed roughly 140,000 collision-avoidance manoeuvres in six months.<br><b>Changed for the game:</b> the States, the companies, the \"seventeen warnings\" and the \"stale orbital data\" are all fictional.",
