"15 秒里，点金色的空轨位抢先申报；蓝色是闲置被收回的轨位，分更高；<b>千万别点红色</b>，那是别人正在用的。":"In 15 seconds, tap the golden empty slots to file first; blue slots are idle ones being reclaimed and score higher; <b>never tap red</b>: those are in use by others.",
"1976 · 赤道上空的一圈轨道":"1976 · One ring of orbit above the equator",
"你点中了别人已经登记、正在使用的轨位。在国际电联的规则下，这叫<b>有害干扰</b>，后来的一方必须让开。<br>":"You tapped a slot already filed and in use by someone else. Under ITU rules that is harmful interference, and the later party must yield.<br>",
"地球静止轨道上的卫星和地球一起转，从地面看一动不动，非常适合通信和气象。但这样的位置只有一圈。":"A satellite in geostationary orbit turns with the Earth and looks motionless from the ground, ideal for communications and weather. But there is only one such ring.",
"地球静止轨道只有一圈，轨位由国际电联按“[[先申报先协调]]”的原则安排；申报了却长期不用，会被收回。1976 年，八个赤道国家发表《波哥大宣言》，主张自己头顶上那段轨道归自己。主张没被接受，但它问了一个好问题：后来的国家，还能分到什么？":"There is only one geostationary ring, and its slots are arranged by the ITU on the principle of first to file, first to coordinate; filed but long unused, they are reclaimed. In 1976, eight equatorial States issued the Bogotá Declaration, claiming the arc above their heads. The claim was not accepted, but it asked a good question: what is left for the States that come later?",
"轨位争夺":"Race for the slots",
"金色＝空轨位　红色＝别人在用　蓝色＝闲置收回":"Gold = empty slot  Red = in use  Blue = idle reclaimed",
